The key to piloting Clive, Ifrit's Dominant is understanding its core engine: Clive discards your hand to draw cards equal to your devotion to red on entry, then transforms into Ifrit, Warden of Inferno to fight creatures and generate 8 red mana over two lore chapters before resetting to draw a fresh hand.
This is a Bracket 3 build running three Game Changers: Jeska's Will, The One Ring, Underworld Breach. It contains zero mass land denial and focuses on high-synergy board development, interactive answers, and an inevitable endgame clock.

# Commander and Core Synergy
Clive, Ifrit's Dominant :: primary commander driving the deck's core strategy
Fanatic of Mogis :: critical engine card maximizing commander synergy and card advantage
Purphoros, God of the Forge :: critical engine card maximizing commander synergy and card advantage
Torbran, Thane of Red Fell :: critical engine card maximizing commander synergy and card advantage
Neheb, the Eternal :: critical engine card maximizing commander synergy and card advantage
Nykthos, Shrine to Nyx :: critical engine card maximizing commander synergy and card advantage

# High-Impact Engines and Support
Birgi, God of Storytelling :: premier support piece providing board presence, ramp, or recursion
Blasphemous Act :: premier support piece providing board presence, ramp, or recursion
Chaos Warp :: premier support piece providing board presence, ramp, or recursion
Deflecting Swat :: premier support piece providing board presence, ramp, or recursion
Ruby Medallion :: premier support piece providing board presence, ramp, or recursion

# Game Changers and Interaction
Jeska's Will :: high-power Game Changer providing irreplaceable tempo, draw, or board control
The One Ring :: high-power Game Changer providing irreplaceable tempo, draw, or board control
Underworld Breach :: high-power Game Changer providing irreplaceable tempo, draw, or board control
